From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:03:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/14] MTP draft head as INT4 g32 records behind
 G6_DRAFT_HEAD_I4

G6_DRAFT_HEAD_I4=1 (default 0, needs --mtp): at boot every rank converts its
MXFP8 lm_head records (G.lm_head.mx.gv) into INT4 g32 GEMV records of the same
vocab slice on the GPU (kernels/head_i4.cuh, records::int4_quantize on the
MXFP8 values; DEC_I4PAIR builds repack them for the launch's ks), and the MTP
draft model's head binds them instead (head_for). 3456 B per vocab row instead
of 6336: the draft head reads 134 MB instead of 246 MB per step at TP4. The
target's head and every verify step are unchanged, so the committed tokens
are the target's; drafts and their log-probabilities can differ from the
MXFP8 head's and stay identical on every rank (same conversion per slice,
head merge in rank order). G6_DRAFT_HEAD_KS / G6_DRAFT_HEAD_TPC set the GEMV
split; all three go into the S2 runtime signature. m4sim reads the same knob.

Offline (E9 held-out roots, 9548 K2 anchors, 288 prompts, qualified layer-78
reference): first-draft acceptance -0.07 pt [-0.32, +0.17], K2 tokens/round
-0.0010 [-0.0056, +0.0034] against the MXFP8 head.

dhead_i4_test (c1_tests.sh): the conversion against a host derivation of the
record layouts, the INT4 head GEMV against a host dot, and --time for the
MXFP8 vs INT4 head GEMV split table.
